ONEDRAFT
CAD-AI — Aria Powered
Backup, Disaster Recovery & Business Continuity
Version 1.0
Status: Implementation Specification
System: OneDraft
Database: PostgreSQL
Artifact Storage: Object Storage
Execution: Runtime Orchestrator + Job & Worker Execution System
Recovery Model: Transactional, Versioned, Immutable and Reconstructable
Primary Objective: Preserve the ability to recover OneDraft project state, generated artifacts, operational services and system configuration following hardware failure, software failure, data corruption, security incident, infrastructure loss or regional service interruption.

1. PURPOSE
The OneDraft Backup, Disaster Recovery & Business Continuity subsystem establishes the mechanisms required to preserve and restore the operational integrity of the OneDraft platform.
The system must protect:
Project data
Project model state
Revision history
Geometry references
Compliance manifests
Validation results
Generated drawings
Document packages
Audit events
Identity and authorization state
Configuration
Infrastructure state
Operational metadata
Recovery must preserve the provenance chain established by the preceding OneDraft architecture.
The objective is not merely to restore files.
The objective is to restore a known, internally consistent OneDraft system state.

2. RECOVERY PRINCIPLE
OneDraft recovery shall operate according to the principle:
BACKUP
 ↓
VERIFY
 ↓
DETECT FAILURE
 ↓
ISOLATE
 ↓
RESTORE
 ↓
RECONCILE
 ↓
VALIDATE
 ↓
RESUME
A successful database restore without corresponding artifact recovery is not considered a complete recovery.
Likewise, restored artifacts without their associated model, revision and provenance state are not considered a complete recovery.

3. BUSINESS CONTINUITY OBJECTIVE
The platform shall maintain continuity of the following core capabilities:
AUTHENTICATION
ORGANIZATION ACCESS
PROJECT ACCESS
PROJECT MODEL
REVISION HISTORY
COMPLIANCE STATE
VALIDATION STATE
DRAWING GENERATION
DOCUMENT GENERATION
ARTIFACT RETRIEVAL
ARIA OPERATIONS
AUDITABILITY
Non-critical derived services may be restored after the transactional project foundation.

4. RECOVERY DOMAINS
The recovery architecture shall distinguish:
DATABASE RECOVERY
ARTIFACT RECOVERY
APPLICATION RECOVERY
WORKER RECOVERY
QUEUE RECOVERY
CONFIGURATION RECOVERY
IDENTITY RECOVERY
SECRETS RECOVERY
OBSERVABILITY RECOVERY
INFRASTRUCTURE RECOVERY
Each recovery domain shall have an explicit restoration procedure.

