141. RECOVERY AND COMPLIANCE PROVENANCE
Recovered compliance manifests shall preserve the original source versions and retrieval timestamps.
A current code source must not be substituted for the historical source used by a prior validation without explicit creation of a new manifest.

142. RECOVERY AND MODEL PROVENANCE
The project model remains the authoritative computational source.
Derived artifacts are recoverable consequences of the model.
Therefore the recovery system prioritizes:
MODEL
 ↓
REVISION
 ↓
VALIDATION
 ↓
DOCUMENTATION
rather than treating PDFs as the sole project record.

143. RECOVERY RECONSTRUCTION PRINCIPLE
If an artifact is lost but the authoritative model and sufficient generation metadata remain available, the artifact should be regenerated.
If the authoritative model is lost, artifact recovery alone is insufficient to reconstruct the full computational project state.

